WEBVTT

00:00:00,660 --> 00:00:06,660
Hi, this is Anne from Conner's Clinic, and in this video we're going to walk you through how to use the computer.

00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:13,660
So when you get your box that contains all the right equipment, the computer is one piece that equipment.

00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:22,660
So the computer is a laptop, it might not look exactly like the one that I have in front of me, but it's going to look similar and the functionality is going to be the same.

00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:27,660
So there's obviously going to be a charging cord for the computer.

00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:34,660
So you might have the cord on right side or the left side, so you'll just have to look to see where the power plug in, the spot is.

00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:40,660
And then you're going to want to have the cord plugged into your search protector.

00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:44,660
So let's just get that plugged in.

00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:51,660
Alright, so once it is the computer is plugged in, you're just going to open up the computer, and then you're going to want to power the computer on.

00:00:51,660 --> 00:00:56,660
So the power button on this version of the laptop is right here.

00:00:56,660 --> 00:01:01,660
Sometimes it might be in the upper right side, sometimes it might be on either side here.

00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:09,660
So you'll have to locate the power button, and then you just hold it down for a couple seconds, and the computer screen should turn on like that.

00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:12,660
Now this is the track pad.

00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:19,660
So in order to move the cursor, you're just dragging your finger along this track pad, and you can see that the cursor is moving.

00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:28,660
So if you just tap anywhere on the screen, it should bring you to this sign-in page, so you just tap on this sign-in button.

00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:35,660
So on this track pad, you can just tap on the middle, or we have these right and left click buttons here.

00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:46,660
Not all of the track pads are going to have these buttons, distinguished buttons, but the track pad, you can just click on, and that will work as a clicker.

00:01:46,660 --> 00:01:53,660
So one thing you'll want to note about the track pad is right-clicking and left-clicking.

00:01:53,660 --> 00:02:00,660
So you can see on this track pad, there's distinct buttons to indicate a right-click or a left-click.

00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:10,660
Not all of the track pads have those. Sometimes you'll just have to right-click in the lower right corner of the track pad, but on this computer we have these distinct buttons.

00:02:10,660 --> 00:02:18,660
So you have to select whatever the left-click button is to select something.

00:02:18,660 --> 00:02:24,660
So right now I have this hovered over John Doe, and I'm left-clicking on this left button.

00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:29,660
And you can see it puts a little check mark there, or sometimes it's just going to highlight what you've selected.

00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:36,660
You can use the left button's upper or lower on this track pad.

00:02:36,660 --> 00:02:42,660
The right button is to bring up another menu option where you can copy and paste.

00:02:42,660 --> 00:02:47,660
So I just right-clicked there, and we have this. So you can copy.

00:02:47,660 --> 00:03:01,660
So in the event that you are getting new files that you want to upload to your true rife frequencies, the program, we will give you instructions, but this is just an example of why you would be right-clicking.

00:03:01,660 --> 00:03:08,660
You're right-clicking to copy, and then you select with the left side.

00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:13,660
So you've right-click to open up this menu, and then you want to select copy.

00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:20,660
And so you left-click on copy, and then you would hit on the documents tab.

00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:28,660
You're left-clicking to select this, and now you are going to left-click again on this.

00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:36,660
Yeah, we're highlighting this, and we're going to right-click to bring up that menu again, and then we want to paste.

00:03:36,660 --> 00:03:47,660
So we're hovering over paste, and then we're going to left-click to select it, and that pastes the new programs into the true rife folder.

00:03:47,660 --> 00:03:55,660
Now, if your programs are named the same thing, it may ask you if you want the new files to overwrite the old files.

00:03:55,660 --> 00:04:02,660
That is fine. Sometimes we're naming the new programs something different, so it's not going to erase the old files.

00:04:02,660 --> 00:04:07,660
It's just going to make a new file with the new programs.

00:04:07,660 --> 00:04:12,660
And so that's an example of when you would want to use a right-click to copy your paste.

00:04:12,660 --> 00:04:18,660
Left-click is always to select whatever you're hovering over what you have highlighted.

00:04:18,660 --> 00:04:22,660
So I hope that helps clarify the trackpad for people.

00:04:22,660 --> 00:04:36,660
Another thing that you can do if the trackpad is confusing, and you're used to using a mouse, you can plug a mouse into the USB drive here, and then you can use the mouse to navigate the computer's phrase.

00:04:36,660 --> 00:04:41,660
You don't have to use the trackpad, so that's an option as well.

00:04:41,660 --> 00:04:52,660
The computer has the videos, so these are the instructional videos that will walk you through setting up the rife machine, setting up the ion pro wave.

00:04:52,660 --> 00:05:00,660
There's also some educational videos on there that you'll want to watch, and then this over here is the true rife icon.

00:05:00,660 --> 00:05:08,660
So that's what you're going to be clicking into in order to get your programs loaded and running.

00:05:08,660 --> 00:05:17,660
So when you receive your computer, we are putting it in airplane mode. You can see there's a little icon down here that looks like an airplane.

00:05:17,660 --> 00:05:23,660
And so you don't need internet to run any of your rife programs.

00:05:23,660 --> 00:05:28,660
You don't need to do any software updates or virus install any virus protection.

00:05:28,660 --> 00:05:33,660
Really, you're just using this computer to run your rife programs and you don't need internet.

00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:46,660
So you can keep it on airplane mode. The only time you would need to connect to wi-fi would be a couple, maybe three times a year, if you want to update the general programs that are provided by true rife.

00:05:46,660 --> 00:05:53,660
So you would connect to your wi-fi by clicking on that little airplane, and then there's this wi-fi button here.

00:05:53,660 --> 00:05:59,660
You would just click on that and then turn or put your password into connect to your wi-fi.

00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:08,660
And then we'll show you how to update the rife frequencies in the rife training video, but that's how you connect to wi-fi.

00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:20,660
Back to the power button. So it is good, maybe one time a week, if you can pick a day of the week, maybe Sunday morning, you're going to wake up and you're going to completely power down the computer.

00:06:20,660 --> 00:06:31,660
It just helps to kind of reset things and prevent any miscommunications between the rife and the computer if you're completely powering the computer down every so often.

00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:40,660
So pick a day of the week where it's convenient and then power down the rife machine. You can do that by holding this power button down.

00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:47,660
If you just tap it, it's going to put it into sleep mode and you certainly can obviously close the computer.

00:06:47,660 --> 00:06:58,660
But we want to do a full power down of the computer so it resets. So I'm just waking it back up, was sleeping.

00:06:58,660 --> 00:07:09,660
Now if I want to do a complete power down, I can either put my cursor over here and highlight over the little windows icon and click on it.

00:07:09,660 --> 00:07:18,660
Then hit this little circle with a line through it, button that says power. So I can hit that and I can do a shutdown.

00:07:18,660 --> 00:07:35,660
And that will power down the computer or you can just hold this power button down for a good, you know, 15 seconds until power is completely down.

00:07:35,660 --> 00:07:42,660
Then you can give it 30 seconds and then start it back up again and that should reset the computer.

00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:52,660
One thing you'll notice on the side of your computer here is these USB ports. So you have one, typically they'll have one on either side.

00:07:52,660 --> 00:08:02,660
So there's one on this side, there's also one on the other side. That you'll be using a USB cord to run from your computer to the rife machine.

00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:10,660
And then also if there's any time where you're receiving a flash drive from us with updated programs or changes to your programs,

00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:19,660
the flash drive will plug into this USB port and there'll be instructions provided on how to install those new programs.

